/**
 * Team AI Allowance: OpenCode in-session plugin.
 *
 * This file is the source for `dist/plugin/team-ai-allowance.ts`. It is
 * deliberately dependency-free apart from Node built-ins, so the built file
 * can be dropped into a managed OpenCode config without an install step.
 *
 * It enforces, for one session:
 *   - a session budget: notices at the configured ratios (50% and 80% by
 *     default), a hard stop at 100%;
 *   - an unattended rule since the last human message: 30 minutes or 40 steps
 *     in working hours, 10 minutes or 15 steps off-hours;
 *   - a loop rule: the same tool + argument hash 5 times, or the same error 3
 *     times.
 *
 * Policy comes from `GET /api/me/session-policy`, cached with a fallback to the
 * last known policy. If that route is not deployed yet, the plugin derives the
 * budget from `GET /api/me` and keeps the built-in unattended and loop rules.
 *
 * Privacy: the state file holds counters, ids, timestamps, costs and hashes.
 * It never stores prompt text, assistant text, tool arguments or tool output.
 */

